<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<paragraphs xml:id="para-project-conventions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Project Conventions &amp; Metadata</title>
  <p>
    Custom styles, metadata formats, and authoring standards used across this networked Zettelkasten:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <title>Note Metadata Blocks</title>
      <p>
        Every note includes a metadata block containing a timestamp Note ID and topic tags. This can be authored in an <c>&lt;introduction&gt;</c>, <c>&lt;blockquote&gt;</c>, or <c>&lt;paragraphs&gt;</c>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <alert>Preview:</alert>
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          <tag>202606012315</tag> | <tag>quantum mechanics</tag>, <tag>linear algebra</tag> | <alert>Interactive:</alert><tag>🔗 Graph Node</tag>
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <program language="xml">
        <code>
          <![CDATA[
<!-- Introduction Metadata Block -->
<introduction>
  <p>
    <tag>202606012315</tag> |
    <tag>quantum mechanics</tag> <tag>linear algebra</tag>
  </p>
</introduction>

<!-- Or using a Blockquote (always visible) -->
<blockquote>
  <p>
    <tag>202606012315</tag> |
    <tag>quantum mechanics</tag>
  </p>
</blockquote>
          ]]>
        </code>
      </program>
    </li>
    <li>
      <title>Note IDs &amp; Glassmorphic Pills</title>
      <p>
        Use <c>YYYYMMDDHHMM</c> or <c>YYYYMMDDNNNN</c> timestamps. The first <c>&lt;tag&gt;</c> in an introduction or blockquote is automatically styled as a glowing purple glassmorphic Note ID badge. Subsequent tags render as cyan topic pills.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <title>Conclusion Metadata &amp; Networked Links</title>
      <p>
        Conclusions use <c>&lt;alert&gt;</c> tags for metadata labels (e.g. Linked Notes, References), which render as glassmorphic pills and populate the D3.js knowledge graph.
      </p>
      <p>
        <alert>Preview:</alert>
      </p>
      <blockquote>
        <p>
          🖇️ <alert>Linked Notes:</alert> <xref ref="sec-pretext" />
        </p>
        <p>
          🔖 <alert>References:</alert> <xref ref="ch-cheat-sheets" />
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <program language="xml">
        <code>
          <![CDATA[
<conclusion>
  <p>
    🖇️ <alert>Linked Notes:</alert> <xref ref="sec-pretext" />
  </p>
  <p>
    🔖 <alert>References:</alert> <xref ref="ch-cheat-sheets" />
  </p>
</conclusion>
          ]]>
        </code>
      </program>
    </li>
    <li>
      <title>List Headings &amp; Assemblages</title>
      <p>
        Titles within list items (<c>&lt;li&gt;&lt;title&gt;...&lt;/title&gt;&lt;/li&gt;</c>) are styled in prominent cyan heading typography. Use <c>&lt;assemblage&gt;</c> blocks for standalone concept takeaways and key formulas.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</paragraphs>
